The issue is also there with `@model_validator(mode="before")` (I assume also with mode=after), it will call the validators of the subclass before the parent class, which is the opposite of what should happen in my opinion, the base class functionality is the foundation of the subclass, therefore the base class validators should get called before the subclass

```py
class Animal(BaseModel):
    name: str

    @model_validator(mode="before")
    def test1(self):
        print("CALL 1")
        return self

class Dog(Animal):

    @model_validator(mode="before")
    def test2(self):
        print("CALL 2")
        return self

d = Dog(name='bob')
CALL 2
CALL 1
```

In part reaction on @pmalic , and I know this is also related to #8277 and #12168 , the way this ordering is happening in V2 seems to be consistent that:
1. from outside to inside (start with child, then go to parents)
2. start with "wrap" and when "handler()" is used go to underlying handlers.
3. then "before" and "after" in order of 1. (only done when "handler" is used, and usually desired).

Our problem is that we started with Pydantic V1 and we align more with ordering used there.
In V1 the parent/root validators are ran before any child, so any child builds on top of what is already there. 
We still have not migrated to V2 due to this change in ordering, which is in a way expected,
even though the ordering is inconsistent it has not been mentioned anywhere;
not in the migration guide and not in documentation of V1 or V2 (very scarcely).
We would like to see the ordering of V1 back.

Below we show V1 and V2 behaviour elaborately, in both cases version 2.12.5 were used:
```
# V1
Comp model-before
Root model-before
      Child model-before
Root field-before
Comp field-before
      Child field-before
Nested model-before
Nested model-after
Root field-after
Comp field-after
      Child field-after
Comp field-before
Root field-before
      Child field-before
Comp field-after
Root field-after
      Child field-after
Comp model-after
Root model-after
      Child model-after
```

